1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,420
You walk into the ATM.

2
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:02,900
The guard is asleep.

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:05,000
The AC is on full blast.

4
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,440
You put in your card, and ten seconds later,

5
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,620
money comes out of a wall.

6
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:11,710
But in those ten seconds, your card, a tiny

7
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:13,810
computer, two banks, and a network you've

8
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,930
never heard of, all hold a quick meeting.

9
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,760
Oh, and at the very end, there's a two second

10
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,940
pause that stops every heart in India.

11
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,420
Let's start with the card.

12
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,740
That gold square is not decoration.

13
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,220
It's a tiny computer.

14
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,780
The old magnetic stripe shouts the same

15
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,260
details every single time, so crooks could

16
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,080
copy it.

17
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,660
The chip makes a brand new secret code for

18
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:35,580
every transaction.

19
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:37,780
Copy it, and it's already useless.

20
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,380
Card read.

21
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,500
Next, the PIN.

22
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:43,760
You type your PIN.

23
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,000
And you cover the keypad with your other

24
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,820
hand, like it's an exam paper.

25
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,060
Good.

26
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,080
But here's the twist.

27
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,940
Your PIN never travels as four numbers.

28
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,740
The keypad has its own little security chip.

29
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,300
The moment you press enter, it scrambles

30
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:00,960
your PIN into a coded block that looks like

31
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:01,780
gibberish.

32
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,120
If someone tries to open the keypad to peek,

33
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:05,480
it wipes its own keys.

34
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,340
Only your bank can unscramble that block.

35
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:09,500
Not the ATM.

36
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:10,920
Not the guard.

37
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:12,320
Definitely not the guard.

38
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,140
He's asleep.

39
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:18,253
Now the ATM sends a message:

40
00:01:19,073 --> 00:01:20,888
card ending four eight two one wants two

41
00:01:20,908 --> 00:01:22,013
thousand rupees.

42
00:01:22,573 --> 00:01:24,813
But what if this ATM belongs to a different

43
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:25,553
bank?

44
00:01:25,573 --> 00:01:26,573
It doesn't know you at all.

45
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:27,733
So it calls a switch.

46
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:30,413
In India, that's the National Financial

47
00:01:30,433 --> 00:01:32,853
Switch, run by NPCI.

48
00:01:33,193 --> 00:01:35,053
It connects over thirteen hundred banks

49
00:01:35,073 --> 00:01:37,133
and about two and a half lakh ATMs.

50
00:01:37,813 --> 00:01:39,933
The switch reads your card number, finds

51
00:01:39,953 --> 00:01:42,013
out which bank you belong to, and forwards

52
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:43,013
the message there.

53
00:01:43,413 --> 00:01:44,553
All in under a second.

54
00:01:44,873 --> 00:01:47,013
And for this little favour, your bank pays

55
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:49,433
the ATM's bank a fee called interchange.

56
00:01:49,453 --> 00:01:51,733
Nineteen rupees per withdrawal.

57
00:01:54,832 --> 00:01:57,072
Your bank unscrambles the PIN, and checks

58
00:01:57,092 --> 00:01:58,352
the chip's secret code.

59
00:01:58,932 --> 00:02:00,012
Then three quick questions.

60
00:02:00,652 --> 00:02:01,452
Enough balance?

61
00:02:01,692 --> 00:02:02,652
Under the daily limit?

62
00:02:03,072 --> 00:02:03,872
Card not blocked?

63
00:02:04,192 --> 00:02:04,992
Three yeses.

64
00:02:05,172 --> 00:02:05,972
Approved.

65
00:02:06,172 --> 00:02:08,112
Your bank holds two thousand rupees, and

66
00:02:08,132 --> 00:02:10,032
the reply races back, through the switch,

67
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:10,852
to the ATM.

68
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:14,092
Your phone buzzes: two thousand rupees debited.

69
00:02:14,572 --> 00:02:15,852
The money has left your account.

70
00:02:16,372 --> 00:02:17,872
It just hasn't left the machine yet.

71
00:02:20,966 --> 00:02:23,086
Now the ATM opens its safe.

72
00:02:24,166 --> 00:02:25,746
Inside are cassettes stacked with notes.

73
00:02:26,466 --> 00:02:28,346
Five hundreds, two hundreds, one hundreds.

74
00:02:29,086 --> 00:02:30,846
Rollers pick the notes one by one.

75
00:02:31,426 --> 00:02:33,606
A sensor checks every note, so two stuck

76
00:02:33,626 --> 00:02:34,846
together don't sneak out.

77
00:02:35,266 --> 00:02:37,066
Any doubtful note goes straight into the

78
00:02:37,086 --> 00:02:37,886
reject bin.

79
00:02:38,226 --> 00:02:39,126
The notes are stacked.

80
00:02:39,526 --> 00:02:40,726
The shutter thinks about it.

81
00:02:41,086 --> 00:02:42,666
And then: please collect your cash.

82
00:02:43,166 --> 00:02:43,966
That pause?

83
00:02:44,066 --> 00:02:45,446
Every heart in India stops.

84
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,846
And if the cash never comes out, but your

85
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:50,626
account is debited, RBI rules say your bank

86
00:02:50,646 --> 00:02:52,806
must return it within five days, or pay

87
00:02:52,826 --> 00:02:55,066
you a hundred rupees for every day of delay.

88
00:02:55,966 --> 00:02:56,766
Card back.

89
00:02:56,786 --> 00:02:57,586
Cash out.

90
00:02:57,726 --> 00:02:58,526
Receipt printed.

91
00:02:58,886 --> 00:02:59,686
Ten seconds.

92
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:00,646
Done.
